# GitHub OAuth Configuration
# 
# To enable GitHub authentication, you need to create a GitHub OAuth App:
# 1. Go to https://github.com/settings/developers
# 2. Click "New OAuth App"
# 3. Fill in the application details:
#    - Application name: promptArq (or your preferred name)
#    - Homepage URL: http://localhost:5173 (for development) or your production URL
#    - Authorization callback URL: http://localhost:5173/auth/callback (for development)
# 4. After creating the app, copy the Client ID and generate a Client Secret
# 5. Create a .env file in the root directory and add the values below

# GitHub OAuth App Client ID (required)
VITE_GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=your_github_client_id_here

# GitHub OAuth App Client Secret (required)
# ⚠️ SECURITY WARNING: Client secrets should never be exposed in client-side code.
# For production, implement a backend proxy to handle token exchange securely.
# This is acceptable for local development only.
VITE_GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET=your_github_client_secret_here

# OAuth Redirect URI (optional - defaults to current origin + /auth/callback)
# VITE_GITHUB_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:5173/auth/callback

# Additional Notes:
# - The app will run in Spark mode if available, otherwise it will use GitHub OAuth
# - User data is stored locally using SQLite for persistence
# - For production deployment, consider implementing a secure backend OAuth flow
